  bootwright / secret set
      Store one declared contextStore secret using the exact input flags for its type.
      Stdin-backed replacement requires --yes.

  Usage
    bootwright secret set [flags]

  Command flags
      --certificate-file  Read a certificate or CA bundle from a file
      --name              Select the exact object name (required)
      --password-file     Read a password from a file
      --password-stdin    Read a password from standard input
      --private-key-file  Read a private key from a file
      --public-key-file   Read an SSH public key from a file
      --username          Store this username with a password
      --value-file        Read a value from a file
      --value-stdin       Read a value from standard input
      --yes               Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright secret set --name token --value-file ./token --yes
